@startuml
title Tickframe Dynamic View - Live Market Update Sequence
autonumber

legend right
  Dynamic-view notation
  Lifeline = runtime participant/component
  Solid arrow = synchronous call or direct handoff
  Dashed arrow = async event, pushed update, or returned data
  The scenario is non-trivial because it crosses exchange, backend,
  database, metrics, WebSocket, frontend, and observability boundaries.
endlegend

participant "React terminal" as UI
participant "FastAPI WebSocket\nendpoints" as API
participant "MarketDataService" as Service
participant "Binance or Bybit\npublic stream" as Exchange
participant "Exchange collector" as Collector
queue "Trade queue" as Queue
participant "CandleAggregator" as Aggregator
participant "LiveStore" as Store
database "TimescaleDB" as DB
participant "Metrics engine" as Metrics
participant "Observability" as Obs

UI -> API : Open market, candle,\nand metrics WebSockets
API -> Service : Wait for stream\nrevision changes
Exchange --> Collector : Trade message over\npublic WebSocket
Collector -> Collector : Parse exchange-specific payload
Collector -> Service : Enqueue canonical Trade
Service -> Queue : Put Trade
Queue --> Service : Consume Trade
Service -> Store : Update market freshness state
Service -> Aggregator : Add Trade to candle window
Service -> DB : Persist raw trade
Service -> Obs : Record exchange-to-backend latency
Service --> API : Notify market and candle revisions
API --> UI : Push latest market and candle payloads
Aggregator --> Service : Finalized stable candle after\nallowed lateness window
Service -> Store : Save stable candle snapshot
Service -> DB : Persist candle revision
Service -> Metrics : Queue metric recomputation
Metrics -> DB : Read candle history when needed
Metrics --> Service : Return metrics, events,\nand correlations
Service -> DB : Persist metric points and\nlatest summary
Service --> API : Notify stable candle and\nmetric revisions
API --> UI : Push stable candles and\nmetric snapshot
UI -> API : POST display-latency 
API -> Obs : Record frontend display latency
@enduml
